726:<li><p>Categories are inferred from the data.</p></li>
727:<li><p>Categories are unordered.</p></li>
730:of <code class="xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">CategoricalDtype</span></code>.</p>
731:<div class="highlight-ipython notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="gp">In [26]: </span><span class="kn">from</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nn">pandas.api.types</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">CategoricalDtype</span>
735:<span class="gp">In [28]: </span><span class="n">cat_type</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">CategoricalDtype</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">categories</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="s2">&quot;b&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;c&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;d&quot;</span><span class="p">],</span> <span class="n">ordered</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="kc">True</span><span class="p">)</span>
746:<span class="go">Categories (3, str): [&#39;b&#39; &lt; &#39;c&#39; &lt; &#39;d&#39;]</span>
749:<p>Similarly, a <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">CategoricalDtype</span></code> can be used with a <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">DataFrame</span></code> to ensure that categories
751:<div class="highlight-ipython notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="gp">In [31]: </span><span class="kn">from</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nn">pandas.api.types</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">CategoricalDtype</span>
755:<span class="gp">In [33]: </span><span class="n">cat_type</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">CategoricalDtype</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">categories</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="nb">list</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s2">&quot;abcd&quot;</span><span class="p">),</span> <span class="n">ordered</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="kc">True</span><span class="p">)</span>
766:<span class="go">Categories (4, str): [&#39;a&#39; &lt; &#39;b&#39; &lt; &#39;c&#39; &lt; &#39;d&#39;]</span>
775:<span class="go">Categories (4, str): [&#39;a&#39; &lt; &#39;b&#39; &lt; &#39;c&#39; &lt; &#39;d&#39;]</span>
781:categories for each column, the <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">categories</span></code> parameter can be determined programmatically by
782:<code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">categories</span> <span class="pre">=</span> <span class="pre">pd.unique(df.to_numpy().ravel())</span></code>.</p>
784:<p>If you already have <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">codes</span></code> and <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">categories</span></code>, you can use the
785:<a class="reference internal" href="../reference/api/pandas.Categorical.from_codes.html#pandas.Categorical.from_codes" title="pandas.Categorical.from_codes"><code class="xref py py-func docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">from_codes()</span></code></a> constructor to save the factorize step
789:<span class="gp">In [38]: </span><span class="n">s</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">pd</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">Series</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">pd</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">Categorical</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">from_codes</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">splitter</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">categories</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="s2">&quot;train&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;test&quot;</span><span class="p">]))</span>
816:<span class="go">Categories (3, str): [&#39;a&#39;, &#39;b&#39;, &#39;c&#39;]</span>
833:strings; categories will end up the same data type as the original values.</p>
838:creation time. Use <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">categories</span></code> to change the categories after creation time.</p>
842:<section id="categoricaldtype">
843:<span id="categorical-categoricaldtype"></span><h2>CategoricalDtype<a class="headerlink" href="#categoricaldtype" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h2>
846:<li><p><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">categories</span></code>: a sequence of unique values and no missing values</p></li>
849:<p>This information can be stored in a <code class="xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">CategoricalDtype</span></code>.
850:The <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">categories</span></code> argument is optional, which implies that the actual categories
852:<a class="reference internal" href="../reference/api/pandas.Categorical.html#pandas.Categorical" title="pandas.Categorical"><code class="xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">pandas.Categorical</span></code></a> is created. The categories are assumed to be unordered
854:<div class="highlight-ipython notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="gp">In [45]: </span><span class="kn">from</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nn">pandas.api.types</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">CategoricalDtype</span>
856:<span class="gp">In [46]: </span><span class="n">CategoricalDtype</span><span class="p">([</span><span class="s2">&quot;a&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;b&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;c&quot;</span><span class="p">])</span>
857:<span class="gh">Out[46]: </span><span class="go">CategoricalDtype(categories=[&#39;a&#39;, &#39;b&#39;, &#39;c&#39;], ordered=False, categories_dtype=str)</span>
859:<span class="gp">In [47]: </span><span class="n">CategoricalDtype</span><span class="p">([</span><span class="s2">&quot;a&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;b&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;c&quot;</span><span class="p">],</span> <span class="n">ordered</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="kc">True</span><span class="p">)</span>
860:<span class="gh">Out[47]: </span><span class="go">CategoricalDtype(categories=[&#39;a&#39;, &#39;b&#39;, &#39;c&#39;], ordered=True, categories_dtype=str)</span>
862:<span class="gp">In [48]: </span><span class="n">CategoricalDtype</span><span class="p">()</span>
863:<span class="gh">Out[48]: </span><span class="go">CategoricalDtype(categories=None, ordered=False, categories_dtype=None)</span>
866:<p>A <code class="xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">CategoricalDtype</span></code> can be used in any place pandas
872:<code class="xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">CategoricalDtype</span></code> when you want the default behavior of
873:the categories being unordered, and equal to the set values present in the
875:<code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">dtype=CategoricalDtype()</span></code>.</p>
879:<p>Two instances of <code class="xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">CategoricalDtype</span></code> compare equal
880:whenever they have the same categories and order. When comparing two
881:unordered categoricals, the order of the <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">categories</span></code> is not considered. Note
882:that categories with different dtypes are not the same.</p>
883:<div class="highlight-ipython notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="gp">In [49]: </span><span class="n">c1</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">CategoricalDtype</span><span class="p">([</span><span class="s2">&quot;a&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;b&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;c&quot;</span><span class="p">],</span> <span class="n">ordered</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="kc">False</span><span class="p">)</span>
886:<span class="gp">In [50]: </span><span class="n">c1</span> <span class="o">==</span> <span class="n">CategoricalDtype</span><span class="p">([</span><span class="s2">&quot;b&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;c&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;a&quot;</span><span class="p">],</span> <span class="n">ordered</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="kc">False</span><span class="p">)</span>
889:<span class="go"># Unequal, since the second CategoricalDtype is ordered</span>
890:<span class="gp">In [51]: </span><span class="n">c1</span> <span class="o">==</span> <span class="n">CategoricalDtype</span><span class="p">([</span><span class="s2">&quot;a&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;b&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;c&quot;</span><span class="p">],</span> <span class="n">ordered</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="kc">True</span><span class="p">)</span>
894:<p>All instances of <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">CategoricalDtype</span></code> compare equal to the string <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">'category'</span></code>.</p>
899:<p>Notice that the <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">categories_dtype</span></code> should be considered, especially when comparing with
900:two empty <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">CategoricalDtype</span></code> instances.</p>
915:<div class="highlight-ipython notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="gp">In [56]: </span><span class="n">cat</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">pd</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">Categorical</span><span class="p">([</span><span class="s2">&quot;a&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;c&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;c&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">np</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">nan</span><span class="p">],</span> <span class="n">categories</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="s2">&quot;b&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;a&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;c&quot;</span><span class="p">])</span>
937:<section id="working-with-categories">
938:<span id="categorical-cat"></span><h2>Working with categories<a class="headerlink" href="#working-with-categories" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h2>
939:<p>Categorical data has a <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">categories</span></code> and a <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">ordered</span></code> property, which list their
941:exposed as <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">s.cat.categories</span></code> and <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">s.cat.ordered</span></code>. If you don’t manually
942:specify categories and ordering, they are inferred from the passed arguments.</p>
945:<span class="gp">In [61]: </span><span class="n">s</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">cat</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">categories</span>
952:<p>It’s also possible to pass in the categories in a specific order:</p>
953:<div class="highlight-ipython notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="gp">In [63]: </span><span class="n">s</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">pd</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">Series</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">pd</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">Categorical</span><span class="p">([</span><span class="s2">&quot;a&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;b&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;c&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;a&quot;</span><span class="p">],</span> <span class="n">categories</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="s2">&quot;c&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;b&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="s2">&quot;a&quot;</span><span class="p">]))</span>
955:<span class="gp">In [64]: </span><span class="n">s</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">cat</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">categories</span>
969:<p>The result of <a class="reference internal" href="../reference/api/pandas.Series.unique.html#pandas.Series.unique" title="pandas.Series.unique"><code class="xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">unique()</span></code></a> is not always the same as <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">Series.cat.categories</span></code>,
970:because <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">Series.unique()</span></code> has a couple of guarantees, namely that it returns categories
972:<div class="highlight-ipython notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="gp">In [66]: </span><span class="n">s</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">pd</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">Series</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nb">list</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s2">&quot;babc&quot;</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">astype</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">CategoricalDtype</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nb">list</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s2">&quot;abcd&quot;</span><span class="p">)))</span>
981:<span class="go">Categories (4, str): [&#39;a&#39;, &#39;b&#39;, &#39;c&#39;, &#39;d&#39;]</span>

